  "articleBody": "Converting an attached or detached garage into usable living space adds valuable square footage, but it requires thorough planning before tools swing. \n\nKey Benefits: You gain an extra bedroom, home office, or guest suite without expanding your home's foundation footprint.\n\nProcess Breakdown: A successful conversion begins by checking local zoning and parking requirements. Next comes drafting architectural plans, closing the overhead door opening with proper framing, adding moisture barriers over the concrete slab, and roughing in sub-trade work like electrical and plumbing. Rough inspections happen before any insulation or drywall goes in, followed by trim, flooring, and final inspection.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice: Deciding whether to create a bedroom versus an office impacts your needs directly. Bedrooms typically mandate egress windows, closet space, and specific fire-life safety measures like smoke detectors.\n\nReady to get your project moving correctly? Contact Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your conversion plans and coordinate your build.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}